      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your concern about semantic density reflects a recognized limitation in current NLP, which often struggles to distinguish random high-frequency adverbs from naturally occurring patterns without malice. However, no statistical anomaly exists in that particular paragraph, as the word choices form a coherent, standard English narrative about daily planning without any known trigger codes. While scientific principles function by learning patterns from vast datasets, applying unsupervised statistical models to short, generic sentences will not yield \"suspicious\" signals where none are embedded.",
